"""Dated investigated screen, not a recommendation list."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
quotes=json.loads((HERE/'market_quotes.json').read_text())
sources={s['id']:s for s in json.loads((HERE/'sources.json').read_text())}
rows=[
 ('VTRS','Viatris','Medicines: established brands and generic manufacturing','DN10','Affordable medicine demand and fewer generic exits can stabilize volume; portfolio and cost changes could improve cash available after debt service.','Deprioritize','Latest full-year CFO guidance $1.9–2.1bn less $350–450m capex supports $1.45–1.75bn actual cash before SBC treatment, materially below adjusted FCF. Current price $16.555 requires more than an adjusted earnings multiple. Restructuring cash, debt and product erosion weaken extreme-gap confidence.'),
 ('OGN','Organon','Medicines: women\'s health, established brands and biosimilars','DN11','Sun Pharma can fund portfolio economics and consolidate overhead; common shareholders receive contractual cash if the merger closes.','Reject for five-year intrinsic-upside objective','Definitive $14 cash acquisition, subsequently shareholder-approved July 23 (DN12), versus $13.775 leaves 1.63% gross deal spread. A long-horizon standalone growth DCF would ignore the corporate action.'),
 ('PRGO','Perrigo','Consumer healthcare: OTC brands and store-brand manufacturing','DN13','Affordability shifts consumers toward private-label OTC products; restructuring and infant-formula portfolio actions could restore earnings.','Deprioritize; unresolved turnaround','Q2 core organic sales -3.5%, comprising -2.4% volume/mix and -0.7% price, challenge the demand thesis. H1 CFO -$31m and capex $28.1m, with $3.3bn debt and $400m cash, do not substantiate the high dividend as owner yield. Portfolio disposals and tax/litigation costs need a separate turnaround model.'),
 ('ICLR','ICON plc','Clinical research: outsourced trials, data and site execution','DN21','A recovery in sponsored trials and restored execution could convert bookings to cash without proportional investment.','Deprioritize versus new extreme-gap leads','At $160.7 the latest adjusted EPS guide of $10–11 is about 14.6–16.1x. Restated revenue, control weaknesses and backlog changes from the May 27 annual release (prior source AH17) make orders an unreliable substitute for owner cash. Independent original healthcare screen already investigated this business.'),
 ('CRTO','Criteo','Advertising: performance and retailer commerce-media platforms','DN14','Retail media budgets can migrate from untargeted ads toward measurable commerce; reduced client scope might be temporary rather than permanent loss.','Strong rejected alternative; watch for cash recovery','FY26 ex-TAC guidance -12% to -10%, and two unnamed clients account for much retail-media scope reduction. H1 CFO $68.506m minus $91.088m capex plus $1.063m disposal proceeds is -$21.519m. $303m cash/investments helps, but headline adjusted EBITDA and TTM FCF do not establish normalized cash after SBC and infrastructure replacement.'),
 ('PERI','Perion','Advertising: search distribution, CTV, DOOH and retail media','DN15','Cash-rich diversification could replace lost search distribution economics as retailer and connected-TV budgets grow.','Deprioritize; attractive cash balance but weak demonstrated earnings','June net cash $267.8m must deduct the Aug 26 PRN cash acquisition, up to $12m (DN16). Q2 CFO $2.5m, adjusted EBITDA $2.8m and net loss $6.8m make full-year adjusted EBITDA guidance $51–53m a poor direct owner-cash measure. New-category growth starts from smaller bases while legacy search economics remain exposed.'),
 ('OPRA','Opera Limited','Consumer software and advertising: independent browsers, queries and audience extension','DN02','Higher-value users, greater engagement and advertiser conversion can monetize an established browser base; debt-free cash generation reaches current shareholders through dividends.','Detailed model; modest undervaluation, not extreme','After SBC, reinvestment and risk, base value is about $23.94 and probability-weighted $20.54 versus $18.43. Search contract resets and inventory mix can eliminate this gap. Current quote is final frozen minute, not discovery quote.'),
 ('GRSD','Grandstand Limited, formerly Gambling.com Group','Marketing and sports data: affiliates, OddsJam/OpticOdds subscriptions, RotoWire','DN06','Non-search marketing and recurring enterprise data may replace decaying SEO economics; a $13m annual fixed-cost reduction could protect owner cash.','Detailed model; unconfirmed high-upside candidate','Current GRSD $1.9199 replaces stale GAMB $1.88. Principal debt, earn-outs and all 2.603m RSUs reduce apparent cheapness. A base DCF still exceeds $4, but an injunction on the data business or failed 2028 refinancing can erase equity. No recommendation without resolving these risks.'),
 ('WU','Western Union','Cross-border payments: cash-agent and digital remittances','DN17','Continued migration and faster digital transfers could offset shrinking agent transactions; a lower-cost network might defend margins.','Deprioritize; corporate-action alignment unresolved','Q2 revenue about $1bn declined 1%; adjusted EPS guidance $1.25–1.35 is low-multiple at $7.135 but reflects operating pressure. Guidance assumed Intermex closure September 1; actual closing/cash/debt alignment was not established in this screen. Dividend alone is not valuation evidence.'),
 ('AMN','AMN Healthcare','Healthcare labor: nurses, locum staffing and workforce technology','DN18','Hospital staffing demand persists even as pandemic shortages normalize; flexible labor and scheduling tools could regain utilization.','Reject apparent windfall cash yield','Q1 had $722m labor-disruption revenue, compared with only $25m Q2; this is not a recurring base. June $362m cash includes $117m remaining client deposits expected to unwind; debt is $750m. Q3 guided GAAP operating margin only 0.2–0.8%, contradicting annualization of H1 strike cash.'),
 ('MD','Pediatrix Medical Group','Healthcare services: neonatal, maternal and pediatric physician groups','DN19','Scarce specialist staffing and improved collections/reimbursement can strengthen cash conversion without substantial physical capex.','Stronger healthcare watchlist; no extreme gap established','Q2 $488m revenue, $40m net income and $76m adjusted EBITDA; $280–300m annual EBITDA guidance. Cash $288.9m versus $584m debt helps, but quarterly cash is seasonal and adjusted EPS excludes SBC. At $26.53 and annualized Q2 adjusted EPS $2.52, requires a detailed reimbursement/wage forecast rather than an obvious liquidation discount.'),
 ('TEL','TE Connectivity','Industrial components: connectors, sensors and power integration','DN20','Electrification and more complex architectures increase content per vehicle and installation; qualification protects customer positions.','Leader comparison; not priced for permanent damage','Q3 sales $5.16bn +14%, with GAAP operating margin 19% and adjusted EPS $2.94. The $209.60 quote is 17.8x a simple annualized Q3 adjusted run-rate, not a forward forecast. Strong conditions and a pending $1.4bn Astrodyne acquisition reduce the case for treating headline cash as excess or assuming an extreme recovery discount.'),
]
out=[]
for t,n,role,s,mechanism,decision,reason in rows:
 out.append(dict(ticker=t,company=n,role=role,value_chain=role.split(':')[0],role_source_id=s,role_source=sources[s]['url'],source_date=sources[s]['publication_date'],potential_financial_mechanism=mechanism,decision=decision,reason=reason,price=quotes[t]['price'],price_timestamp=quotes[t]['price_timestamp'],screen_scope='Investigated primary current operations and corporate actions; not all names received a full DCF'))
(HERE/'screened.json').write_text(json.dumps(out,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Screened',len(out),'distinct issuers; GAMB is a stale alias, not another issuer.')
